# CLINE - DIRECTORY-STRUCTURE

Purpose:
- State the recommended modular project organization so the AI assistant can reason about file locations and responsibilities.

Top-level structure:
- docs/
  - literature/
  - architecture.md
  - technical.md
  - product_requirement_docs.md
- tasks/
  - rfc/
  - active_context.md
  - tasks_plan.md
- src/
- test/
- utils/
- config/
- data/
- .clinerules/
  - rules
  - plan
  - implement
  - debug
  - memory
  - directory-structure

Notes:
- Keep documentation in docs/ (PRD, architecture, technical).
- Keep active, short-term context in tasks/active_context.md so the assistant uses it as working memory.
- Store formal proposals in tasks/rfc/.
- Use .clinerules/ to hold the assistant rules and workflows.
- Add .gitkeep files in otherwise-empty directories to ensure they are preserved in VCS if needed.
